WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.930
India, more than a thousand years ago.

2
00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:06.920
A philosopher named Shankara
studies the ancient Upanishads.

3
00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:11.880
He finds in them one startling teaching,
and builds a whole philosophy on it.

4
00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:15.750
His boldest claim: only
one reality exists,

5
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.780
one without a second.

6
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:21.610
But look around: trees, people, stars.

7
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:26.780
If only one reality exists, why do we
see a world full of separate things?

8
00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.750
In this mission, you'll
meet that one reality,

9
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.900
Brahman, and the words
Shankara uses for it.

10
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:37.180
Then you'll see why his followers
speak of different levels of reality.

11
00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:42.450
Your mission: find out how Shankara
explains a world of many separate things.
